{
  "UniqueId": "Cornucopia.MoreCrops",
  "CheckedVersion": "1.6.3",
  "Notes": "Custom Bush fruit: a bush bears from AgeToProduce days after planting, in its Seasons and on the days its item Condition names (Custom Bush README); its age is taken to count every day, as a tea bush's does, since the README does not say. | Custom Bush fruit indoors: the README says seasons are ignored in non-seasonal locations, so each bush also gets a GreenhouseCrop route, as reliable as its sapling, the way the data's own greenhouse crop routes are. | Custom Bush fruit week rulings: the week of the outdoor bush route's first dependable landing from day 1, not the greenhouse route's, since the greenhouse waits for the Pantry. | (O)Cornucopia_Peppercorn and (O)Cornucopia_Vanilla: their saplings are dependable only from the Island Trader, so that bush route is GingerIsland and the one from a Traveling Cart sapling is Chance. | SpaceCore spawn groups: every vanilla-map row is gated by If RANDOM p per map per day, so each route is Chance (decision table row 1); the SVE, East Scarp and Sunberry Village rows need those mods and the island rows are not year 1, so they are left out. | Bell pepper colours: SpaceCore's YieldOverrides add each colour with PerItemCondition RANDOM 0.1 to every harvest of the Summer Bell Pepper crop (10 days to the first), so each route is Chance. | RandomShopItems: the Traveler lines Cornucopia.MoreCrops_ExclusiveExtended and _ExclusiveEssential name their item with a {{Random: ...}} token (data/shop_travelingcart.json), so each is listed with every item it can hold. | (O)Cornucopia_Sapodilla: week 5, the first Summer, because its shake condition is an ANY that TLY reads as all year and an outdoor tree only fruits in Summer (data/wildtrees.json). | (O)Cornucopia_Sugarcane: week 9, when the Desert opens, because its seeds (Sandy) and its spawn group are both in the Desert. | Summit spawn rows are kept with location:Summit, as TLY walks the Summit as reachable from week 1.",
